```

> **Note**  
> The naive recursive implementation has exponential time complexity (`O(2^n)`).  
> For large `n` (e.g., `n > 40`) it becomes very slow.  
> If you need to compute large Fibonacci numbers efficiently, consider using memoization, an iterative approach, or matrix exponentiation.
